Open English WordNet — https://en-word.net/
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) the Open English WordNet contributors.

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Grawlix bundles a modified form of the noun.exc and verb.exc inflectional
exception lists from the 2025 release: reduced to lines mapping an irregular
surface form to its base, with forms a suffix rule already reaches removed. No
other WordNet data is used.


wordfreq — https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) Robyn Speer.

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Grawlix bundles a derived word list — the 30,000 most frequent English words
from the large_en corpus, as a bare alphabetical list with frequencies dropped —
used as a tiebreak when reducing entries to word families. It also fetches the
full large_en frequency corpus at runtime for space-out word segmentation.
